{"version":2,"text":"Transfusion Reaction\n\nText A\n\nINVESTIGATING ACUTE TRANFUSION REACTIONS\n\n1. Immediately report all acute transfusion reactions with the exceptions of mild hypersensitivity\nand non-haemolytic febrile transfusion reactions, to the appropriate departments.\n2. Record the following information on the patient’s notes:\n• Type of transfusion reaction\n• Length of time after the start of the transfusion and when the reaction occurre d\n• Volume, type and pack numbers of the blood components transfused\n3. Take the samples and send them to the appropriate laboratory\n• Immediate post -transfusion blood samples from a vein in the opposite arm:\n- Group & Antibody Screen\n- Direct Antiglobulin Test\n- Blood unit and giving set should contain residues of the transfused donor blood\n4. Take the following samples and send them to the Haematology/ Clinical Chemistry Laboratory\nfor:\n• Full blood count\n• Urea\n• Coagulation screen\n• Creatinine\n• Electrolytes\n• Blood culture in an appropriate blood culture bottle\n5. Complete a transfusion reaction report form.\n6. Record the results of the investigations in the patient’s record s for future follow-up, if required.\n\nText B\n\nRELEVANT EFFECTS\n\nBronchodilator\nvasopressor\n\nExpand blood volume\n\nReduce fever and\ninflammatory\nresponse\n\nDRUGS & DOSES\nName\nRoute & Dosage\nOxygen\n60-100%\nAdrenaline\n500 micrograms im\nrepeated after 5 mins\nif no better, or worse\n0.9% - Saline,\nIf patient hypotensive,\nGelufusine\n20ml/kg over 5\nminutes\nParacetamol\nOral or rectal\n10mg/kg\n\nNOTES\n\nst\n\n1 line\nst\n1 line\n\nst\n\n1 line\n\nnd\n\nInhibits histamine\nmediated responses\nInhibits immune\nmediated\nbronchospasm\n\nChlorphenamine\n(Chlorpheniramine)\nSalbutamol\n\nIV 0.1 mg/kg\n\n2 line\nAvoid aspirin\ncontaining products if\npatient has low\nplatelet count\nnd\n2 line\n\nBy 5ml nebuliser\n\n2 line\n\nAminophylline\n\nVasopressor\nbronchodilator\n\nAdrenaline 6mg in\n100ml\n5% dextrose (6%)\n\nUse under expert\nguidance\n5-10ml/hr\n\nPage 310\n\nnd\n\nUse only under expert\nguidance","layout":{"version":1,"width":595.200012,"height":841.919983,"blocks":[{"text":"Transfusion Reaction","lines":[{"text":"Transfusion Reaction","x":0.4255930240135815,"y":0.09681729813508892,"width":0.20647184227543328,"height":0.013184150779326506,"confidence":1,"words":[{"text":"Transfusion","x":0.4255930240135815,"width":0.11582663912983929,"confidence":1},{"text":"Reaction","x":0.5468027477123102,"width":0.08526211857670461,"confidence":1}]}]},{"text":"Text A","lines":[{"text":"Text A","x":0.1496589032326834,"y":0.12389824223948845,"width":0.062016144583007825,"height":0.013184150779326506,"confidence":1,"words":[{"text":"Text","x":0.1496589032326834,"width":0.04173388524730069,"confidence":1},{"text":"A","x":0.19711859649626484,"width":0.014556451319426386,"confidence":1}]}]},{"text":"INVESTIGATING ACUTE TRANFUSION REACTIONS","lines":[{"text":"INVESTIGATING ACUTE TRANFUSION REACTIONS","x":0.1593363123117679,"y":0.14225627543989533,"width":0.3734717700240907,"height":0.013112885099438252,"confidence":1,"words":[{"text":"INVESTIGATING","x":0.1593363123117679,"width":0.12062017733964699,"confidence":1},{"text":"ACUTE","x":0.28385164414277597,"width":0.051360501316656565,"confidence":1},{"text":"TRANFUSION","x":0.3390516699115927,"width":0.10212738537377584,"confidence":1},{"text":"REACTIONS","x":0.4450371348446814,"width":0.08777094749117721,"confidence":1}]}]},{"text":"1. Immediately report all acute transfusion reactions with the exceptions of mild hypersensitivity\nand non-haemolytic febrile transfusion reactions, to the appropriate departments.\n2. Record the following information on the patient’s notes:\n• Type of transfusion reaction\n• Length of time after the start of the transfusion and when the reaction occurre d\n• Volume, type and pack numbers of the blood components transfused\n3. Take the samples and send them to the appropriate laboratory\n• Immediate po